cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Mandara OS in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "Mandara OS"
abstract: >-
  Mandara OS is a hyper-optimized, bloat-free Linux distribution: an
  image-based Fedora desktop operating system tuned for software development
  and everyday personal use, published as a bootable container image (bootc)
  for x86_64 and aarch64 with installer ISOs and ready-made virtual machine
  disks. On x86_64 it runs the CachyOS LTO kernel with the sched-ext scx_lavd
  scheduler; it builds the MangoWM compositor from source with ThinLTO and
  CPU-specific flags, uses Btrfs with zstd compression, installs no weak
  dependencies, and ships a ready Rust and container toolchain. Its desktop
  is Mandara Shell, and a new image is built automatically for every Mandara
  Shell release.
type: software
